A Style's `cursor` on fyne, a Look's Cursor shown over the node's box.

Fyne styles no widget's cursor, and the field was listed as not answered.
A box now carries a pointer area a desktop driver asks for its cursor
(`fynelayout.Box`); a CSS name Fyne has no cursor for is the default arrow,
and an unset one leaves the cursor of the box around it.
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
    }
}

ui.window {
    var busy = false
    ui.vbox(style={cursor="pointer"}) {
        ui.text(value="open")
        ui.input(value="", style={cursor="text"})
        ui.text(value="drag", style={cursor="ew-resize"})
        ui.text(value="wait", style={cursor=(busy ? "wait" : "crosshair")})
    }
}
